    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d414">

                <pb facs="0603" n="483" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg483"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-11-09"><hi rendition="#italic">November 9,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: With reference to the letter
                    which I had the honor to receive from Mr. Loomis, dated September 26, on the
                    subject of the preservation of Niagara Falls, I have the honor to inform you
                    that the substance of Mr. Loomis’s communication was referred to the
                    governor-general of Canada, with a request for an expression of his views on the
                    subject.</p>
                <p>This action had already been taken prior to the receipt of your letter of
                    November 3, the substance of which I have communicated to Lord Lansdowne.</p>
                <p>Believe me, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. M. Durand.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
